  "corrected_mechanism": "Google Trends normalises each single-term query to its own 0-100 max, so absolute search volume is structurally invisible in every series this project has collected. The zero fraction is the one proxy that survives normalisation: a series rounds to 0 only when the underlying counts are tiny. STZ's raw series is dense, but its earnings-intent series is zero in 95% of weeks. The thinness is in the earnings-attention construct, not the raw ticker series.",
  "defeating_normalisation_requires": "a single multi-term build_payload, which normalises ACROSS terms -- a network call, not attempted here"
 },
